-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  cpp_placement.pcpp - C++ integration compliance: cpp header; and cpp source;

  Plain mixed C++ at module level goes to the source file unless
  `cpp header;` sends what follows to the header; `cpp source;` switches
  back (BNF.md sec 10). Both stand at module level only.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\cpp_placement.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\cpp_placement.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    header 8
    source 9
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  The [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.

  Break it: run each file below the same way, without -r; each reports
  exactly what the // comment on its marked line says, and nothing else:
    cpp_placement_err_target.pcpp
      cpp takes header or source (PR0015)
    cpp_placement_err_body.pcpp
      cpp header; inside a body (PR0050)
*******************************************************************************/

module exe cpp_placement;

cpp header;
inline int Quadruple(int AValue) { return AValue * 4; }

cpp source;
int Triple(int AValue) { return AValue * 3; }

begin
  println("header {}", Quadruple(2));
  println("source {}", Triple(3));
end.
